anon wrote:
>
> After losing two more wizards this week to a giant mimic and a rope
> golem, I'm wondering what is the best way to survive a grabbing attack.

Mimic grabs - Learn various ways to avoid them in the
first place.  Mimics never grab you unless you hit
them first.  Once you know which objects are mimics
and which are not, they aren't a problem until they
start appearing in the main dungeon not in a shop.

Rope golem - Kill them with your wielded weapon.  Rope
golems aren't particularly powerfull and by the time
my characters encounter them they aren't an issue.
This does require all the usual tactics of watching
your hit points and never engaging in combat if they
are below maybe half, not getting into crowds of
anything but corpses and so on.

Christopher mentioned entering and leaving a shop to
find the mimics.  I distictly remember that happening
in some version and I didn't even notice when it
stopped happening.  It's only one of several methods
of detecting mimics.  My favorite method is watching
my pet kill them until I'm powerfull enough to handle
a large mimic on my own.


